# Scalable Architecture Gate

This repo is mid-migration toward single-source-of-truth modules. We do NOT
rewrite existing code wholesale. But for anything we **touch or add**, we must
consciously choose the scalable path and **ask the user first**.

The canonical map of what exists today is `module-registry.md` (same folder).
**Always read it before answering** and keep it updated when modules/features change.
Module vs feature definitions and target structure live in `module-architecture.mdc`.

A **domain spans layers** (frontend `app/src` + backend `server/src` + Supabase).
Before changing a domain, look it up in the registry and check whether your change
touches the other layers — keep one shared contract, not a separate one per layer.

## Always pause and ask first

Before writing any scalable refactor, STOP and ask the user to confirm. This
applies even to small refactors. State the trade-off (effort vs. scalability)
and let the user decide. Never silently restructure code.

If the user declines, make the minimal in-place change and note the debt.

## When ADDING something new

Before creating files, classify the work and tell the user your classification:

1. **Module** = a business/domain area that owns its code (e.g. `affiliate`,
   `catalog`, `checkout`, `admin`). New business area → new module.
2. **Feature** = a capability inside an existing module (e.g. `admin/orders`).
   New capability in an existing area → feature in that module.

Then ask: "This looks like a `<module|feature>` named `<x>`. Add it the
scalable way (own `types` + data access + public `index.ts`), or quick in-place?"

Check `module-registry.md` first — the area may already exist under a different name.

## When TOUCHING existing code

If the file is in a fragmented domain (see registry "Fragmented" column),
surface it: "`<domain>` is fragmented across `pages/`, `components/`, `context/`.
We could promote the part we're touching into a module. Proceed scalable, or
patch in place?" — then wait for the answer.

## Single-source-of-truth checklist (raise before proceeding)

- Redefining `Product`/`Category`/`Order`/`CartItem`/affiliate shapes locally? → reuse the shared/generated type.
- Adding a new `supabase.from(...)` call inside a component? → route through a domain API/hook.
- Adding a second registry/config for something that already has one? → extend the existing source.

## After any structural change

Update `module-registry.md` so it stays the source of truth, and run
`npm run type-check` in the affected package before committing.
